-- A call script for examples/lists.lang (kit slice K4c): cons writes and nil on a List field, and folds over it.
-- nil on the empty List, then three cons writes (one word, two words, one word). The view paidSum is the sum;
-- the view weighted gives the elements as digits from the last element to the head; settle writes the sum to tally.
-- settleWith 5u writes 5 plus the sum to tally (a fold over cons 5u on the field); paidSum shows the List did not change.
-- The view over is the max word at tally 0 (now 99) and traps at tally 25 (now 113): a view that traps (O-c4-3).
99 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb over
100 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb wipe
101 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
102 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushOne 7u
103 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
104 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushTwo 9u
105 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
106 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb weighted
107 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb pushOne 3u
108 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
109 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb weighted
110 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb settle
111 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb settleWith 5u
112 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb paidSum
113 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000000bb over
